From: Uke Linux maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: admit the exact Uke camera VIO resource

MiCode kernel_devicetree 94c84aeb and camera-devicetree 57d2135
route the front EEPROM VIO to PMXR2230 L20B, resource ldob20.
Admit only that resource. Preserve command-DB/type/mode validation,
the shared provider constraints and native error ownership.
The read-only at24 consumer owns its separate 1.8 V request.

--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
@@ -2014,7 +2014,8 @@
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob8") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldod3") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldoe7") &&
-	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "bobb1"))
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "bobb1") &&
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob20"))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	aggr_vreg->addr = cmd_db_read_addr(aggr_vreg->resource_name);
